comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-13T09:41:11.342Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 2756-item all-status export and request-specific telemetry queue/concurrency searches found no active owner for missing start delivery. The closed flush-receipt predecessor covers truthful drain counts, not cross-process event preservation. This intake records observed evidence without claiming an established root cause or remediation."
  "2026-09-13T21:19:08.864Z","harness:codex","Live scope evidence: complete CLI export read all 2757 items across open draft closed and canceled statuses with zero omissions or unreadable items. Existing canonical telemetry and closed flush-receipt lineage reused. GitHub has zero open PRs and zero open Dependabot code-scanning or secret-scanning alerts; all six open issues already include canonical PM links. Source inspection identifies process-local queue serialization and two stale retention rewrites; isolated subprocess negative controls are being executed before closure."
  "2026-09-13T21:34:53.119Z","harness:codex","Continuation authorized: user approved takeover of the prior session claim. Current bootstrap and 40 focused tests pass, including independent-process event preservation and loopback collector lifecycle pairing. Full all-status CLI export contains 2757 items with complete reads and no omissions. GitHub has no open PRs or security alerts; all six open issues have canonical PM links. Full coverage and static validation are running; no completion or publication is claimed."
  "2026-09-13T21:40:20.269Z","harness:codex","Connected tranche now includes pm-yjq2x0: isolated SDK negative controls exposed stale completion capture after persisted consent revocation. Focused verification passes 78 tests after the guard. Dependency disposition: npm audit has zero vulnerabilities; the four outdated major entries map to pm-do5b, pm-fokyhh, and pm-ksr40d. Installed CodSpeed supports Vitest 3/4, typescript-eslint supports TypeScript below 6.1, and npm-package-arg 14 requires a higher runtime floor than the published Node 22.18 contract. No compatible wanted upgrade remains."
  "2026-09-13T21:41:19.953Z","harness:codex","Live release and observability checks: scheduled auto-release run 34745705596 succeeded and published v2026.9.13; npm latest is 2026.9.13. Preserve the existing daily release. Sentry access and threshold checks pass with zero unresolved critical/high issues; required telemetry query reports 2.18 percent finish errors and zero failures missing error codes. These aggregate checks do not prove per-invocation completeness; final paired probes and physical queue inspection remain separate."
  "2026-09-13T21:48:36.062Z","harness:codex","Verification checkpoint: all linked tests pass and independent packed npm/Bun CLI lifecycles plus public SDK persisted-consent acceptance pass. npx/bunx smoke passes. Static providers passed source quality and documentation checks but the token-budget subprocess hit a dist import failure while linked runners rebuilt the same output. Treat that attempt as failed proof; rerun against stable built artifacts without concurrent builds. No gate threshold or timeout was weakened."
  "2026-09-13T21:49:08.738Z","harness:codex","Full coverage attempt failed: 685 suites and 8828 tests passed, but sdk-subpath-entrypoints could not import a removed generated bundle chunk while concurrent linked runners rebuilt dist. No coverage artifact was emitted. Re-running with stable output and no concurrent rebuilds; this is orchestration failure evidence, not a passing coverage result."
  "2026-09-13T22:03:51.214Z","harness:codex","Graph gate identified four prose references introduced by this tranche without corresponding edges. Added associative links for the documented toolchain compatibility decisions and the paired privacy work; they are contextual relationships, not fabricated implementation dependencies. The unchanged base commit reproduces the local CLI latency failures with nearly identical timings, separating this host/base limitation from the telemetry patch."
  "2026-09-13T22:19:17.701Z","harness:codex","Bounded production proof 2026-09-13T22:17:43.806Z through 22:17:45.188Z: four concurrent real CLI get invocations delivered four starts and four finishes, with four exact backend matches by installation, process session, canonical command, and finish started_at. The physical local events queue was zero bytes after flush. This establishes this probe window only, not historical completeness. Typecheck, graph composition, record integrity, and fresh tracked-secret scanning pass; full coverage remains running."
  "2026-09-13T22:26:58.999Z","harness:codex","Final stable-build coverage passed: 687 test files and 8832 tests; statements 64400/64400, branches 49138/49138, functions 13385/13385, lines 61677/61677. Exact coverage gate passed 100/100/100/100. All linked concurrency tests, packed npx/bunx smoke, isolated npm/Bun CLI and SDK acceptance, typecheck, graph composition, record integrity, secret scan, dependency audit, and bounded production pair correlation pass. Hosted review and merge are still pending."
  "2026-09-13T22:39:20.205Z","harness:codex","Final static disposition: ESLint, zero-duplication, source/documentation assurance, contracts, package boundaries, command grammar, refusal negative controls, token checks, tracker context, gate registry, and SDK public surface passed. SDK import-cost rerun passed all 10 entrypoints after a transient 230ms versus 226ms merge-import result. CLI timing still exceeds unchanged local limits for get/context/next/create; the separately built unchanged base reproduces this class of failure. No threshold or waiver changed. Hosted exact-head checks remain required before merge."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-13T21:55:43.438Z","harness:codex","Graph context check used all 2757 live exported records before new intake: every record had at least one parent or dependency connection. Typed lineage already includes implements, discovered_from, verifies, supersedes, recurs_from, blocks, blocked_by, and incident_from. Graph audit returned two informational legacy hierarchy advisories. Enrichment must express evidence-backed semantics; do not inflate edge counts or depth with invented dependencies."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-13T21:21:42.305Z","harness:codex",Atomic rename protects readers from partial snapshots but cannot preserve an append racing between snapshot read and replacement. Appends and every reconciliation or retention rewrite must share the same cross-process transaction boundary; network I/O must remain outside that boundary.
  "2026-09-13T21:51:32.427Z","harness:codex","Build output is shared mutable state. Do not run a build-producing linked test, package smoke, or static gate alongside coverage or import-contract checks in the same checkout: rebuilt hashed chunks can disappear beneath a running consumer. Sequence build producers, then verify stable artifacts; a missing coverage report is failed proof."
